   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to establishing the state police communication interoperability demonstration project",
    "basePrintNo": "S7511",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7511-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Homeland Security",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7511\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act in relation to establishing the state police communication\ninteroperability demonstration project\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill is to authorize the state police to create a communication\ninteroperability demonstration project.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\n§ 1-1 establishes that radio communications problems exist between\nstate and local law enforcement agencies warranting the authorization\nof this interoperability demonstration project.\n\n§ 1-2 defines for the purposes of the communication interoperable\ndemonstration program a geographic area that the state deems most\nappropriate for this program.\n\n§ 1-3 to the extent possible, the state should take into account such\nareas, as defined in § 1-2, that may already contain the necessary\ninfrastructure as to facilitate a more efficient roll-out of the\nprogram.\n\n§ 1-4 defines how the project will be funded through a pre-existing\nfunding source within the New York State Division of Homeland Security\nand Emergency Services.\n\n§ 1-5 allows for the state to determine the best vendor(s) for this\nprogram based on familiarity of the program, readiness to complete in\nthe most cost efficient and timely manner off existing OGS Radio\nContract.\n\n§ 2 - establishes the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nOn June 6, 2015 Richard Matt and David Sweat escaped from the Clinton\nCorrectional Facility in Dannemora. Those involved in the manhunt have\ncitied significant radio communications problems such as coverage\ngaps, no coverage at all, interoperability between the state police\nradios and local and federal radios, and a continued lack of\nencryption.\n\nIt is envisioned that this pilot project will engender the development\nof a test system in one state police Troop, utilizing local and state\ninfrastructure cooperatively, to demonstrate a solution to the\ninteroperability issues which continue to plague the system.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone. This legislation provides for the program to be funded through\nDivision of Homeland Security and Emergency Services.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
